            <ArticleTitle>Fortunoids A-C, Three Sesquiterpenoid Dimers with Different Carbon Skeletons from Chloranthus fortunei.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>734-737</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b00066</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three dimeric sesquiterpenoids (1-3), fortunoid A (1) possessing a new carbon skeleton of rearranged lindenane dimer and fortunoids B (2) and C (3) representing the first example of the dimers of a lindenane and a eudesmane sesquiterpene, were isolated from Chloranthus fortunei. Their structures with absolute configurations were established by spectroscopic data and electric circular dichroism analysis. Their biosynthetic origins were also proposed. Compounds 1 and 2 showed moderate antimalarial activities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
